WEBVTT

00:00:32.259 --> 00:00:34.344
(Aslan) Your Majesty?

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:47.482
We are ready.
Everyone has assembled.

00:00:56.825 --> 00:01:01.204
(Caspian) Narnia belongs to
the Narnians, just as it does to man.

00:01:01.288 --> 00:01:05.542
Any Telmarines who want to stay
and live in peace are welcome to.

00:01:05.625 --> 00:01:08.003
But for any of you who wish,

00:01:08.086 --> 00:01:11.673
Aslan will return you
to the home of our forefathers.

00:01:11.756 --> 00:01:14.801
It's been generations
since we left Telmar.

00:01:14.885 --> 00:01:17.262
We're not referring to Telmar.

00:01:17.345 --> 00:01:20.015
Your ancestors were seafaring brigands.

00:01:20.098 --> 00:01:22.809
Pirates run aground on an island.

00:01:22.893 --> 00:01:28.023
There they found a cave, a rare chasm
that brought them here from their world.

00:01:28.106 --> 00:01:30.859
The same world
as our kings and queens.

00:01:33.528 --> 00:01:35.822
It is to that island I can return you.

00:01:35.906 --> 00:01:39.951
It is a good place for any
who wish to make a new start.

00:01:42.037 --> 00:01:43.163
(man) I will go.

00:01:45.457 --> 00:01:47.083
I will accept the offer.

00:01:54.966 --> 00:01:56.635
So will we.

00:02:01.139 --> 00:02:06.811
Because you have spoken first,
your future in that world shall be good.

00:02:14.986 --> 00:02:17.489
(all exclaiming)

00:02:46.726 --> 00:02:49.437
(crowd murmuring)

00:02:49.521 --> 00:02:51.648
- Where did they go?
- They killed them.

00:02:51.731 --> 00:02:55.443
How do we know he is not
leading us to our death?

00:02:55.527 --> 00:02:59.114
Sire. If my example
can be of any service,

00:02:59.197 --> 00:03:01.992
I will take 11 mice
through with no delay.

00:03:09.082 --> 00:03:13.003
- We'll go.
- We will?

00:03:13.086 --> 00:03:16.298
Come on. Our time's up.

00:03:17.757 --> 00:03:19.718
After all...

00:03:21.094 --> 00:03:23.722
...we're not really needed here anymore.

00:03:28.101 --> 00:03:30.562
I will look after it until you return.

00:03:30.645 --> 00:03:32.689
(Susan) I'm afraid that's just it.

00:03:34.691 --> 00:03:36.443
We're not coming back.

00:03:39.571 --> 00:03:40.614
(Lucy) We're not?

00:03:41.489 --> 00:03:42.782
You two are.

00:03:44.034 --> 00:03:47.704
At least, I think he means you two.

00:03:48.622 --> 00:03:50.582
But why?

00:03:50.665 --> 00:03:53.710
- Did they do something wrong?
- Quite the opposite, dear one.

00:03:53.793 --> 00:03:55.962
But all things have their time.

00:03:56.046 --> 00:03:59.507
Your brother and sister have learned
what they can from this world.

00:03:59.591 --> 00:04:02.218
Now it's time for them
to live in their own.

00:04:04.262 --> 00:04:06.264
It's all right, Lu.

00:04:07.766 --> 00:04:10.602
It's not how I thought it would be...

00:04:10.685 --> 00:04:13.063
...but it's all right.

00:04:13.146 --> 00:04:16.858
One day you'll see, too. Come on.

00:04:51.559 --> 00:04:53.144
I'm glad I came back.

00:04:54.562 --> 00:04:56.648
I wish we had more time together.

00:04:59.109 --> 00:05:01.444
It would never have worked, anyway.

00:05:01.528 --> 00:05:03.238
Why not?

00:05:03.321 --> 00:05:05.949
I am 1,300 years older than you.

00:05:26.803 --> 00:05:30.598
I'm sure when I'm older I'll understand.

00:05:30.682 --> 00:05:33.643
I'm older and don't think
I want to understand.

00:05:34.519 --> 00:05:37.522
(♪ Regina Spektor: The Call)

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.723
Aren't you coming, Phyllis?

00:07:04.025 --> 00:07:06.820
You don't think there's
any way we can get back?

00:07:08.488 --> 00:07:10.240
I've left my new torch in Narnia.

00:07:10.323 --> 00:07:13.409
(all laughing)

00:07:23.795 --> 00:07:27.423
(Aslan roars)

